    "The Lequnshe, located in Liuzhou City, Yufeng District, Liu Shi Road No. 2, is assumed have been the residence of the KPG in the late 1930s for a time. The Lequnshe was a French-style building constructed in the late 1920s by the Russians and used as a bus terminal, and its name changed to ‘Lequnshe’ and began to be used as a hotel.": 1,
    "After the March First Movement in 1919, the patriots that moved the bases of the independence movement abroad saw the need for a stronger independence movement organization to resist the might of the Japanese imperialists. On the evening of November 9, 1919, Kim Won-bong and twelve others formed the Righteous Patriots Corps outside of a Chinese farmer’s house in Jilin Province. After its creation, it resolved to assassinate high officials of the Government-General of Korea, the military leadership, the Government-General of Taiwan, national traitors, pro-Japanese leaders, spies and detectives, and anti-Korean landed proprietors. In the first half of the 1920s it moved its headquarters to Beijing and actively resisted the Japanese.": 1,
    "The Bongodong (Fengwudong) Anti-Japanese Battle Memorial is on the on left of the center path from Tumen City Water Supply’s Front Gate to its dam. Bongodong Lower, Mid, and Upper Villages where the Battle of Bongodong took place were submerged in the construction of the Tumen Reservoir.": 1,
    "The Jiandao Korean Association was formally ratified by the local Chinese authorities on April 1, 1913. This association was the representative anti-Japanese independence movement organization in the northern Jiandao region and expanded and reorganized into the Jiandao Educational Association with Kim Yak-yeon, Kim Yeong-hak, and Jeong Jae-myeon in July 1909. Records show that the former site of the Jiandao Korean Association Headquarters was located in the center of Yanji City in the second floor of the Yanji Government City Hall.": 1,
    "This was the site of the officer training academy which I Dong-hui established around 1914 to prepare for fighting against the Japanese.": 1,
    "This is the site of the Korean National Association of Gematang Town created by Gu Chun-seon and others in 1919.": 1,
    "Song Mong-kyu was born along in the same year as Yun Dong-ju in Mingdong Village and attended the same elementary, middle, and even Yonhi College (Yonsei University) together with him. Song was imprisoned for the crime of holding anti-Japanese ideology while studying in Japan and while serving his sentence, he died in Fukuoka Prison in Japan on March 10, 1945.": 1,
    "Yun Dong-ju participated in the anti-Japanese movement in Japan and died in prison in February 16, 1945. His remains were interred here.": 1,
    "The Japanese imperialists, which had instigated the Hunchun Incident in 1920 October, sent a large number of troops to Jiandao on the pretext of protecting the autonomous people and eliminating mounted bandits there. The main core of the troops sent was the 19th Battalion stationed in Korea. However, the Japanese had already thoroughly prepared a ‘subjugation plan’ against the Korean community in North Jiandao. The Jiandao Tragic Incident was not a sudden incident but a throughly planned massacre. Chaman in Jangamdong was the most representative example.": 1
   },
